{
  "name": "open-hypergraphs",
  "description": "A high-performance Rust library implementing data-parallel algorithms for open hypergraphs and string diagrams as described in contemporary applied category theory research. It facilitates the algebraic construction of multi-input/multi-output operation networks through tensor products and composition, featuring built-in support for functors and optic transformations for reverse differentiation. The implementation provides both a mutable lax interface for term building and a strict, parallelizable representation optimized for large-scale evaluation and automatic differentiation.",
